media.org/wiki/File:Fa%C3%A7ade_Palais_Bourbon_3.jpg","sourceSha1":"8c6bbf9412c3e9aa20fae8c5ca87de6749d8b102","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"North river facade: twelve freestanding columns, shallow projecting entablature and triangular sculptured pediment, raised steps and flanking solid wings"}],"aliases":[],"authors":["Open Landmarks contributors"],"artisticLicense":"CC-BY-4.0","spatialDataLicense":"ODbL-1.0","licenseScope":"CC BY applies to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","assistance":"AI-assisted architectural interpretation and procedural recipe authoring; deterministic Python/Blender export. No photographic textures.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["The complete mapped 81-part ensemble preserves three courtyard voids, the twelve-column north portico, smaller southern colonnades and 27.4 m pediment ridge.","Part heights and roof rises use OSM IGN LiDAR HD tags. Mansard and gambrel roofs use simplified inset profiles; domes, gables and skillion roofs retain their mapped heights.","Reviewed river-front photographs establish the open Corinthian colonnade and triangular pediment; sculptures, column fluting, roof lettering and flags are omitted at map scale.","Approved copper and structural-glass colors distinguish mapped roof materials; actual facade window panels always use light blue.","Sparse inferred window rows are constrained to real mapped wall eaves. There are no facade windows on the mapped columns."],"source":{"url":"/objects/ada7d532704015bfe19dc815b15a75988c1552b69f1f54340c49ae240bfd867d/source.blend.gz","bytes":188241,"sha256":"ada7d532704015bfe19dc815b15a75988c1552b69f1f54340c49ae240bfd867d"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/objects/7defbe3bf87697f0628a3e8b3eb699e6cc26bd1b387dcece3d349d1dd7fa8601/spatial-source.json","bytes":79430,"sha256":"7defbe3bf87697f0628a3e8b3eb699e6cc26bd1b387dcece3d349d1dd7fa8601"},"previ